Integrity was checked before extracting the CommonJS runtime, public declarations,
package metadata and LICENSE.md. The unused ESM bundle is not included.

Controlled dictionary-only changes in dist/fontoxpath.js:
  if(pg[a])return pg[a];
becomes:
  if(Object.hasOwn(pg,a))return pg[a];
In inference context rh and its Yg scope creation, the initial and nested
namespace/variable frames use Object.create(null) instead of {} (four further
substitutions).
In dynamic fontoxpath:evaluate (Qq), the variable identity dictionary changes:
  Object.keys(e).reduce((n,t)=>{n[t]=t;return n},{})
to:
  Object.keys(e).reduce((n,t)=>{n[t]=t;return n},Object.create(null))
This sixth dictionary-only change preserves legal external variable names such
as __proto__ in nested evaluations. No other source is changed.

The original predefined lookup and inference frames treat inherited properties
such as constructor, __proto__ and toString as namespace/variable entries,
bypassing the caller's resolver. These changes also cover dynamically constructed
xs:QName values, without rewriting user XPath or string values. Parsing and
evaluation algorithms are otherwise unchanged. No installed dependency is
monkey-patched and no consumer install/build hook is needed. Direct runtime
dependencies prsc 4.0.0 and xspattern 3.1.0 are pinned by the parent package.

